{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Boards on the window Mail by [E7]the door
[A7]What would anybody leave so [D7]quickly for?
[F]Ophelia
[G7]Where have you [C]gone?[A7][D7][G7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The old neighborhood just ain't the same
Nobody knows just what became of
Ophelia
Tell me, what went wrong    (Just hang on C, no turnaround)
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Was it somethin' that [C]somebody said?
[G7]Mama, I know we broke the [C]rules
[F]Was somebody up [C]against the law?
G7                            G7+5
Honey, you know I'd die for you
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Instrumental Break}
Ashes of laughter
The ghost is clear
Why do the best things always disappear
Like Ophelia
Please darken my door
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
They got your number
Scared and runnin'
But I'm still waitin' for the second comin'
Of Ophelia
Come back home
{end_of_chorus}

